## Generic Number of Axes

Functions can take arrays with a generic number of axes. A name to the axes of the array is assigned as followed:
```
func Add(a float32, b [___S]float32) [S___]float32
```
defines an `Add` function which takes two arguments: a `float32` scalar, and an array of `float32` with generic axes named `S`. `Add` returns an array with the same type (same axes, same data type).

We use the notation `___S` to assign all the axis lengths to the variable `S`. The notation `S___` unpacks the axis lengths. This notation is temporary and will be changed when GX will use its own AST.


```code:main
package main

func Add(a float32, b [___S]float32) [S___]float32 {
    return a+b
}

func Main() ([1][2]float32, [2][3]float32) {
    a := Add(-10, [1][2]float32{{1, 2}})
    b := Add(10, [2][3]float32{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}})
    return a, b
}
```
